+ * Get the ByteBuffer representing the FlatBuffer. Only call this after you've
+ * called finish(). The actual data starts at the ByteBuffer's current position,
+ * not necessarily at 0.
+ *
+ * @returns {flatbuffers.ByteBuffer}
+ */
